/// What a window manager asks of the shell (211-APP-0044). The shell alone holds the operator's authorities (MC-3.11);
/// it lends a client of this interface in SLOT_SHELL to a program that asks for it (REQUEST_SHELL), and a client gets
/// only what the interface offers.
package mind:shell@1.0.0;

interface shell {
    /// Why the shell could not do it: it has no window broker client, or no memory for the window.
    enum error { unavailable, no-memory }
    /// Opens the shell's own window, as Ctrl+Alt+F5 does, unless it is open; answers its id in the window broker, for
    /// the manager to bring it to the front.
    window: func() -> result<u32, error>;
}
